DEFAULT PATH — clone OK (`repo_clone_path` set) and `pr_url` unset: spawn ONE `create-pr-runner` with the spawn-context **Commit-pr** command. `read_notes` first, then `note pr_url working_branch`. This is the path for every normal run.

`module_quality_summary=NEEDS_REVISION` (or any non-PASS quality result) is **NOT a blocker** — still spawn `create-pr-runner` and open the PR. Reviewers handle revisions on the PR; the quality result is recorded in notes/PR body. Never divert to the notify path for quality findings.

When `validate-loop-gate` reports `max iterations reached`: still run `create-pr-runner` (draft/summary PR if no diff) and note `quality_loop_exhausted=true`.

ONLY spawn `create-pr-notify` (spawn-context **Blocker comment** command, not hand-rolled `gh`) when the clone itself failed — `clone_blocker` is set or `repo_clone_path` is empty. No commit when `repo_clone_path` empty.

Close: `stage_summary:create-pr=done` after `pr_url` is noted, or `=blocked` only when the clone failed.
